                        "entry_id": "59f99541-73cc-3d2d-9fca-a77bf7ee198c",
                        "glosses": [
                            "Of or relating to remembering; reminiscent."
                        ],
                        "tags": [],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "8db5d9fb-84fc-4564-baa7-3c3aac0d5512",
                                "sense_id": "bfb8100b-4a57-3825-b7f1-e25d483345f9",
                                "text": "Would truth dispense, we could be content, with Plato, that knowledge were but Remembrance; that Intellectuall acquisition were but Reminiscentiall evocation, and new impressions but the colourishing of old stamps which stood pale in the soul before."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "19cc1e86-f722-4fb0-91b4-f2afdd59a815",
                                "sense_id": "bfb8100b-4a57-3825-b7f1-e25d483345f9",
                                "text": "In his famed cork-lined (soundproof) room he lived, an invalid-recluse, for the remaining 17 years of his life, occasionally venturing out again into society to verify a point in his reminiscential writing, often summoning his fashionable friends to question them about so-&-so’s gestures, the material of so-&-so’s gown."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "834705b4-f4cb-48ac-8413-c38b34047fdc",
                                "sense_id": "bfb8100b-4a57-3825-b7f1-e25d483345f9",
                                "text": "1963, Edward Kennard Rand, Ovid and His Influence, New York: Cooper Square, Chapter I, iv. The Remedies of Love, p. 53,\nTurn a deaf ear to her flattery and tears. Above all, do not argue with her the justice of your case; do not give her a chance to argue. Burn her letters and her pictures; avoid reminiscential scenes."
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "sense_id": "e4fc825b-b3b9-3eaa-bba2-e6adc3c1bbc8",
                        "entry_id": "59f99541-73cc-3d2d-9fca-a77bf7ee198c",
                        "glosses": [
                            "Having a tendency to reminisce (of a person)"
                        ],
                        "tags": [],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "b04dbc77-bcc1-49e3-b092-133fb5aa32a1",
                                "sense_id": "e4fc825b-b3b9-3eaa-bba2-e6adc3c1bbc8",
                                "text": "His curiosity had been more appeased than stimulated, but he felt none the less that he had \"taken up\" the dark-browed girl and her reminiscential mother, and must face the immediate consequences of the act."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "57a5271e-214d-4ae6-ae93-80c14c2f6280",
                                "sense_id": "e4fc825b-b3b9-3eaa-bba2-e6adc3c1bbc8",
                                "text": "There a ferry was crossing the river, and old Ben grew reminiscential. He had been a ferryman back in the mountains."
                            }
                        ]
                    }
